 "extraction": "VizieR ASU TSV export, -out=**&-out.max=unlimited. Cleaned file maps upstream columns to a standard schema (id,ra_deg,dec_deg,z,z_err,q_flag,member_flag) and appends sep_arcmin and R_proj_Mpc computed from the cluster centre with FlatLambdaCDM(H0=70,Om0=0.3). No rows dropped. Where the upstream redshift is stored as a velocity cz in km/s it is converted to z=cz/c and its uncertainty is converted consistently to dz=e_cz/c; otherwise no values are altered. Raw upstream response kept verbatim in raw/.",
 "note": "Abell 2029 (z=0.0773). Tyler, Rieke & Bai 2013, ApJ 773, 86 ('Star-forming galaxies in ACO 2029'). 585 rows, all cluster members ('A2029 member list'). Redshifts are compiled from SDSS and earlier literature, not from a new homogeneous spectroscopic survey; the paper's purpose is 24um/Halpha/FUV star-formation diagnostics, so the redshift information is secondary. Selection function: heterogeneous - treat as a supporting/cross-check catalogue only, superseded by Sohn+2017/2019 for kinematics. Sky coverage to ~43 arcmin (~3.9 Mpc projected).",
